A wren counter tracks nests with this code:
class Nest { static int built = 0; Nest() { built++; } }
Nest a = new Nest(); Nest b = new Nest(); Nest c = new Nest();
System.out.print(Nest.built);
What integer is printed?

A mill ledger updates its shared stock with this code:
class Mill { static int sacks = 2; static void grind() { sacks += 3; } }
Mill.grind(); Mill.grind();
System.out.print(Mill.sacks);
What integer is printed?

A freight depot mixes private and shared stock:
class Depot { static int crates = 10; int id; Depot(int n) { id = n; } int total() { return id + crates; } }
Depot a = new Depot(1); Depot b = new Depot(5);
System.out.print(b.total());
What integer is printed?

An aviary census shares one tally:
class Aviary { static int birds = 7; }
Aviary x = new Aviary();
x.birds = 9;
Aviary y = new Aviary();
System.out.print(y.birds);
What integer is printed?

A quarry survey stamps each pit once:
class Quarry { final int depth; Quarry(int d) { depth = d + 1; } }
Quarry q = new Quarry(4);
System.out.print(q.depth);
What integer is printed?

A cannery chains its builders:
class Cannery { int jars; Cannery() { this(4); } Cannery(int j) { jars = j * 2; } }
Cannery c = new Cannery();
System.out.print(c.jars);
What integer is printed?

A foundry picks its pour by signature:
class Foundry { static String cast(int m) { return "cold"; } static String cast(double m) { return "hot"; } }
System.out.print(Foundry.cast(5));
What text is printed?

A lookout guards its lenses yet ends up broken:
class Lookout { public int lenses = 2; void setLenses(int n) { if (n >= 0) { lenses = n; } } }
Lookout o = new Lookout(); o.lenses = -4;
The lookout now holds -4 though the setter forbids negatives. What is wrong?

A hatchery tally misbehaves:
class Hatchery { static int chicks = 0; Hatchery() { chicks = 0; chicks++; } }
Three hatchery objects are built and the shared tally reads 1 instead of 3. What is wrong?

A granary ledger layers class setup above per-sack work:
class Granary { static int sacks = 1; static { sacks = sacks + 2; } Granary() { sacks = sacks * 2; } }
Granary g1 = new Granary(); Granary g2 = new Granary();
System.out.print(Granary.sacks);
What integer is printed?

A harbor report fails to compile:
class Harbor { int buoys = 3; static void report() { System.out.print(buoys); } }
What is wrong with report?

A meadow deed misfires:
class Meadow { final int acres; Meadow(boolean big) { if (big) { acres = 10; } } }
The compiler rejects the constructor. What is wrong?

A nursery picks feeders by widening:
class Nursery { static String feed(long n) { return "cart"; } static String feed(double n) { return "silo"; } }
System.out.print(Nursery.feed(7));
What text is printed?

A rolling library cart leaks quietly:
class LibraryCart { private int[] shelves = {3, 1, 4}; public int[] getShelves() { return shelves; } }
LibraryCart c = new LibraryCart(); c.getShelves()[0] = 99;
The private shelves now start with 99. What is wrong?

A signal yard numbers its towers:
class Signal { static int next = 1; int id; Signal() { id = next; next += 2; } }
Signal s1 = new Signal(); Signal s2 = new Signal(); Signal s3 = new Signal();
System.out.print(s3.id);
What integer is printed?

An observatory parameter shadows its shared tally:
class Observatory { static int stars = 5; static int count(int stars) { return stars + Observatory.stars; } }
System.out.print(Observatory.count(2));
What integer is printed?

A lifeboat yard stamps plates through a shared launcher:
class Lifeboat { static int launched = 0; final int plate; Lifeboat() { launched++; plate = launched * 10; } static Lifeboat launch() { return new Lifeboat(); } }
Lifeboat a = Lifeboat.launch(); Lifeboat b = Lifeboat.launch();
System.out.print(b.plate);
What integer is printed?
